  "merger_description": "Holcim (Australia) Pty Ltd (**Holcim**) proposes to acquire the assets and business of Burdett Group Pty Ltd (**Burdett's**).\n\nHolcim is a Swiss multinational company that supplies building materials. In Australia, Holcim supplies sand and hard rock aggregates, ready-mix concrete (**RMX**), engineered concrete solutions and precast pipes. Holcim supplies RMX under the \u2018Holcim\u2019 and \u2018VicMix\u2019 brands.\n\nBurdett\u2019s is a family-operated business. Its core business is supplying processed extractive sands along with soils and landscaping materials for customers in the South-East of Melbourne. Burdett\u2019s also operates an RMX plant in Langwarrin.  \n\n  \n\nBoth Holcim and Burdett\u2019s supply sand and hard rock aggregates in Southeast Victoria, and RMX in the local area surrounding Langwarrin. Sand and hard rock aggregates are used as inputs into RMX and other products such as glass. RMX has a variety of applications, including in construction and landscaping. There is an existing commercial relationship between the Parties in that Holcim has supplied Burdett\u2019s small volumes of sand on an ad hoc basis and Burdett\u2019s has provided cartage services to Holcim from time to time.",
